================================================================================
                    FRONTEND APPLICATION DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================

1. OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This frontend application is a client-facing web portal for broadband lead generation 
and network coverage verification. It allows users to check internet service coverage 
in real time using GPS geolocation or manual zone selection, select subscription plans, 
and submit leads directly to the UISP CRM backend through the secure Express proxy server.


2. FILE STRUCTURE & ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- index.html:
  * Structure: Contains section landing areas (Hero, Services, Coverage Check, Plans, FAQ, Contact).
  * Lead Modal: Multi-step lead capture modal for Residential and Business inquiries.
  * Form Elements: Collects customer contact info (name, phone, street address, zone).
  * Dynamic Modals: Styled modal popups initialized via SweetAlert2.

- script.js:
  * Application Logic: Handles tab switching, plan selection, and UI interactions.
  * Geolocation Engine: Implements browser `navigator.geolocation` and point-in-polygon 
    polygon checks (`MOCK_COVERAGE_POLYGONS`) to detect user coverage zones (e.g., Tabarre).
  * Form Handler: Sanitizes phone inputs, constructs the lead JSON payload, and posts to 
    the backend endpoint (`/api/leads`).
  * Unified UI Theme: Injects dark-themed CSS styling overrides for SweetAlert2 popups 
    and toast notifications.


3. KEY FUNCTIONALITIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Real-time GPS Coverage Check:
  * Captures browser coordinates (latitude, longitude).
  * Matches coordinates against local boundary polygons (`checkMockCoverage`).
  * Automatically populates and locks the `#zone` input field with the detected zone name 
    or tags "Hors Zone (Liste Prioritaire)" if out of bounds.

- Plan Selection & Tab Switching:
  * Toggles between "Residential" and "Business" customer types.
  * Dynamically updates plan offerings and stores active selection for lead submission.

- Lead Creation Payload:
  * Formats data according to the backend proxy structure:
    - `isLead`: true
    - `clientType`: 1 (Residential) or 2 (Business)
    - `firstName` & `lastName`
    - `contacts`: Phone number and contact flags
    - `street1`: Formatted GPS string or address
    - `city`: Identified coverage zone
    - `note`: Includes selected plan, coverage status, and zone summary


4. BACKEND INTEGRATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Target Endpoint: `POST https://uisp-proxy-ls6j.onrender.com/api/leads`
- Security Requirements: CORS configuration must permit the origin hosting `index.html` 
  (e.g., `https://mystvictor.github.io`).
- Optional Verification: Passes Cloudflare Turnstile token (`turnstileToken`) in the 
  request payload if bot protection is enabled.


5. UI & STYLING OVERRIDES (SWEETALERT2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Custom Dark Theme:
  * Dark Background: `#121026`
  * Primary Accent: `#7c3aed` (Purple buttons)
  * Cancel/Secondary Accent: `#475569` (Slate grey buttons)
  * High Contrast Text: `#ffffff` titles, `#cbd5e1` body text
- Scaled Toast Notifications:
  * Specialized CSS overrides target `.swal2-popup.swal2-toast`.
  * Title Font Size: `0.9rem`
  * Body Font Size: `0.825rem`
  * Compact Padding: `0.6rem 0.9rem` for minimal screen obstruction.